Sparky Stereo OS: a translucent pixel counts in the 3D view's fit at the contribution-weighted mean distance of what it shows (each layer by its share of the pixel's colour, a background seen through a layer at the screen): the measuring pass is drawn twice into a float framebuffer with linear fog from the camera, toward white and toward black, and the difference of the two pictures is that mean at every pixel. Coin draws transparent shapes without writing depth, so a transparent shape nearest the camera was not measured and could pass the popped limit. Without a float framebuffer the transparent shapes write depth in the measuring pass and count at their own distance.
The fit's distances are computed by stereoFitDistances() (src/Gui/View3DStereoFit), with a unit test in FreeCAD's Gui_tests_run (View3DStereoFit), which the recipe runs from the build tree.
The Framebuffer render type keeps one picture per eye, each drawn with its own camera after the fit: both eyes had shown one picture in that type.
